UPSTREAM ATTRIBUTION

rag-mcp-servers is a collection of independent MCP server projects built on UltraRAG plus a reusable companion UI library:

    UltraRAG
    https://github.com/OpenBMB/UltraRAG
    https://ultrarag.openbmb.cn/

UltraRAG's upstream README identifies it as a joint project of THUNLP at Tsinghua University, NEUIR at Northeastern University, OpenBMB, and AI9stars, together with the wider UltraRAG contributor community:

    https://nlp.csai.tsinghua.edu.cn/
    https://neuir.github.io/
    https://www.openbmb.cn/home
    https://github.com/AI9Stars
    https://github.com/OpenBMB/UltraRAG/graphs/contributors

UltraRAG supplies the MCP architecture, tools, prompts, pipeline design, chunking, indexing, and retrieval foundations used by the projects collected here. UltraRAG is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and its license contains the notice "Copyright 2023 OpenBMB":

    https://github.com/OpenBMB/UltraRAG/blob/main/LICENSE.txt
    https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Each server submodule contains a version-specific NOTICE identifying the exact UltraRAG revision on which it depends and a suggested software citation. The UI submodule contains its own ecosystem acknowledgement and does not bundle an UltraRAG runtime.

